  "hindi": "सोने में गन्ध, गन्ने के दण्ड में फल, चन्दन का पुष्प निश्चय ही नहीं बनाया गया; विद्वान्, धन से सम्पन्न और चिरायु राजा; पहले कोई विधाता को बुद्धि देने वाला नहीं हुआ।",
  "english": "Fragrance in gold, fruit in the sugarcane stalk, a flower of the sandal tree: not made, indeed; a learned man rich in wealth, and a long-lived king; formerly no one was a giver of intelligence to the Creator.",
  "text_flags": [
   {
    "src": "nākari",
    "suggest": "nākāri",
    "why": "possible: the aorist passive of √kṛ is akāri (long ā), so na akāri gives nākāri; the printed form has a short a"
   }
  ],
  "notes": "The verb 'was not made' (na akāri) stands in line b; it is understood for the other items (gandha, phala, puṣpa) and, in this reading, also for the learned rich man and the long-lived king (lines c); the Sanskrit has no verb in c. dhātuḥ is read as a genitive of the Creator ('to/for the Creator'); an ablative reading is possible. Whether ca joins vidvān with dhanāḍhya or the two persons with the king is ambiguous.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
